# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime SQLite databases (backend)
#
# These are state the running app writes, not source. Every one of the seven
# was tracked, so simply starting the backend marked popularity.db and quiz.db
# modified and swept them into unrelated commits — and a binary file is the
# worst possible thing to hit a merge conflict on once more than one person is
# committing.
#
# Nothing seeds them. Each owning router calls `_init()` at import time and
# every table is `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`, so a missing file is recreated
# empty on the next backend start. The quiz's questions are generated in
# Python from live standings; `quiz.db` only ever held `attempts`.
#
# users.db additionally holds password hashes, salts and live session tokens,
# which should not have been in version control at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
f1-dashboard/backend/*.db
